Capture build only: never apply this to src/ or commit it.

The SDK 4.44 emulator's time_ms() steps back about 990 ms once a second, so the app redraws stale
digits in a recording. Real watches do not do this: a probe sampling time_ms() every 10 ms on
hardware saw 12000 samples and no step back. Apply this to a throwaway copy of the app:

  git archive HEAD | tar -x -C /path/to/copy
  cd /path/to/copy && patch -p1 < .../tools/screencap/epoch_guard.patch

--- a/src/c/utility.c
+++ b/src/c/utility.c
@@ -100,5 +100,13 @@
 uint64_t epoch(void) {
   time_t sec;
   const uint16_t ms = time_ms(&sec, NULL);
-  return (uint64_t)sec * 1000 + ms;
+  // CAPTURE BUILD ONLY: the SDK emulator's time_ms() steps back ~990 ms once a second (real
+  // watches don't), so a sub-second step back is held at the last reading
+  static uint64_t last;
+  const uint64_t now = (uint64_t)sec * 1000 + ms;
+  if (now < last && last - now < 1000) {
+    return last;
+  }
+  last = now;
+  return now;
 }
